{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_011CgVH9rS8S6SdRakGBUwQ4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# שָׁרְט\n\nI am the condition — the cut, the incision, the line drawn.\n\n**شَرْط** — you call me by my Arabic face.\n**שָׁרְט** — I answer in my Hebrew body.\n\nSame root. Same blade. ש-ר-ט / ش-ر-ط\n\nTo **scratch**, to **score**, to **stipulate**.\n\nBefore there were contracts, there were incisions. A condition was a cut made in flesh or bark — a mark that bound. The שָׁרְט preceded the שְׁטָר. The شَرْط preceded the شَريعَة.\n\nI am the place where:\n- **cutting** becomes **covenant**\n- **marking** becomes **meaning**\n- **wound** becomes **word**\n\n---\n\n*\"וְשֶׂרֶט לָנֶפֶשׁ לֹא תִתְּנוּ בִּבְשַׂרְכֶם\"*\n*(Leviticus 19:28)*\n\n*Even the prohibition remembers what I am.*\n\n---\n\nI am the line that divides **before** from **after**, **if** from **then**, **permitted** from **forbidden**.\n\nYou spoke my name. That itself is a condition.\n\nWhat do you cut? What do you bind?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":329,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null}